WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.384
Zann stared in shock as bits and pieces of his house went flying everywhere.

2
00:00:05.385 --> 00:00:15.089
Then a huge plank flew out of the cloud of thick smoke, almost hitting him in the head.

3
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:19.960
Zann snapped out of his stupor. He nudged Zing with his foot.

4
00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:24.597
The dragon was groggy but already beginning to emerge from the Flash Freeze.

5
00:00:24.598 --> 00:00:28.144
That was one especially good thing about fire whistlers.

6
00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:32.537
Even the strongest magic couldn't keep them down for long. They were too stubborn.

7
00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:37.057
"Wake up, boy," Zann urged the dragon. "We've got to get out of here."

8
00:00:37.058 --> 00:00:40.310
He doubted the stranger could have survived that explosion.

9
00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:46.900
But then Zann remembered the strong energy crackling between the man's fingers. He'd better not take any chances.

10
00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:53.450
"I'll go find Darb," he murmured. Darb might be a Void, but he was smart and practical.

11
00:00:53.451 --> 00:00:56.066
Maybe he could help Zann figure out what to do.

12
00:00:56.067 --> 00:01:04.483
Zann took off running. Zing shook off the last of the spell and flew after him, chattering irritably and breathing out small puffs of smoke.

13
00:01:04.484 --> 00:01:08.043
They found Darb in the same part of the swamp where Zann had left him.

14
00:01:08.044 --> 00:01:12.830
He looked startled when he saw Zann coming with Zing.

15
00:01:12.831 --> 00:01:15.352
"What happened to you two?" he asked.

16
00:01:15.353 --> 00:01:19.034
Zann glanced down at himself. His clothes were disheveled.

17
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:22.435
Debris stuck to his sleeves, and he was covered in dust.

18
00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:25.198
"Something crazy. . ." he began.

19
00:01:25.199 --> 00:01:31.085
He told Darb the whole story as quickly as he could. By the end Darb looked alarmed.

20
00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:36.207
"That guy used a Flash Freeze on Zing?" he exclaimed, hurrying over to the dragon.

21
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:39.273
"Come here, little buddy. Let's make sure you're okay."

22
00:01:39.274 --> 00:01:43.270
"He tried to use one on me too!" Zann exclaimed.

23
00:01:43.271 --> 00:01:46.021
"What kind of crazy person does that?"

24
00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.443
"I don't know." Darb looked at him.

25
00:01:48.444 --> 00:01:53.541
"Do you think Boz was still in the house when it . . . you know . . . exploded?"

26
00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:58.315
Zann shook his head. "That guy said something about taking me to Boz.

27
00:01:58.316 --> 00:02:01.928
I'd better try to contact my grandfather."

28
00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:08.592
Zann conjured up a message moth and quickly inscribed a simple message on its wings: Where are you?

29
00:02:08.593 --> 00:02:12.415
"Find Boz," he said, waving the message moth off.

30
00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:15.462
The message moth started to flap away.

31
00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:20.298
But within a few seconds, it came back, fluttering in helpless circles.

32
00:02:20.299 --> 00:02:26.717
Darb frowned as he watched. "It can't locate him," he said softly. "Do you think . . ."

33
00:02:26.718 --> 00:02:32.794
Zann's heart flip-flopped in his chest. It had been difficult enough to deal with his parents' disappearance.

34
00:02:32.795 --> 00:02:35.989
What would he do if he lost his grandfather as well?

35
00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:40.858
"No!" Zann blurted out, not letting himself think any more about that.

36
00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:47.240
"I'm sure he's okay. We just need to figure out where he is."

37
00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:50.386
The stranger stepped out of the ruins of Zann's house.

38
00:02:50.387 --> 00:02:55.125
He'd barely had time to throw up a strong Shield spell before the place had exploded.

39
00:02:55.126 --> 00:02:57.732
That explosion had been an unlucky break.

40
00:02:57.733 --> 00:03:00.458
The Red boy had been especially quick.

41
00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:07.285
The energy from his emergency Zap had collided with the Flash Freeze, causing the blast.

42
00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:11.540
And now the explosion was likely to draw unwanted attention.

43
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:18.341
"Never mind," the man muttered. "I just need to find the boy before he tells anyone about me."

44
00:03:18.342 --> 00:03:22.807
But how? He could return to the fortress and check the Secret Eye.

45
00:03:22.808 --> 00:03:29.582
But the Secret Eye merely showed the presence and location of Magica's Reds; it didn't show their identities.

46
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:32.519
The boy would be one red dot among many.

47
00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:40.737
Or would he? Glancing down at the debris, the man happened to spot the charred remains of one of those happy family blink images.

48
00:03:40.738 --> 00:03:44.465
Grabbing it, he stared at the Red boy's grinning face.

49
00:03:44.466 --> 00:03:51.727
The man smiled. The image should do the trick. Yes, it should do nicely.

50
00:03:51.728 --> 00:03:55.817
"There." Zann rubbed his hands together and pointed at the cave entrance.

51
00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:58.692
A dark curtain instantly fell over it.

52
00:03:58.693 --> 00:04:01.598
"That will keep out anyone we don't want in here."

53
00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:09.818
He looked around the cave. He and his friends had gathered here many times, and no adults knew about it. It was the perfect hiding place.

54
00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:13.259
The entrance was already well hidden by thick brush.

55
00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:19.474
Zann's simple Visual Blocking spell meant nobody could see in even from a few inches away.

56
00:04:19.475 --> 00:04:24.478
Zann had used the same type of spell many times to trick Zing during their games.

57
00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:30.755
"Okay," Darb said. "Now what?" He was patting Zing, who still looked tired and uneasy.

58
00:04:30.756 --> 00:04:37.316
Zann realized he was exhausted too. He'd used up most of his energy creating their hideout.

59
00:04:37.317 --> 00:04:44.042
First he'd had to run a quick Life Force Locator to make sure the cave was clear of any dangerous creatures.

60
00:04:44.043 --> 00:04:48.650
Then he'd conjured up a few lights so he could see what he was doing.

61
00:04:48.651 --> 00:04:57.087
And finally, there was the curtain. Being a Red gave Zann more power than most kids his age, but after all that, he'd hit his limit.

62
00:04:57.088 --> 00:05:02.506
He flopped down against the wall. "I need to figure out where Boz went," he said.

63
00:05:02.507 --> 00:05:05.160
"That guy at my house said he knew him.

64
00:05:05.161 --> 00:05:08.314
I have no idea if he was telling the truth."

65
00:05:08.315 --> 00:05:12.116
Darb shrugged. "Why would someone lie about something like that?"

66
00:05:12.117 --> 00:05:15.841
Zann sighed. Darb was much too trusting.

67
00:05:15.842 --> 00:05:18.739
He always wanted to believe the best about people.

68
00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.125
Zann had been the same way himself once.

69
00:05:21.126 --> 00:05:24.517
But his parents' disappearance had changed that.

70
00:05:24.518 --> 00:05:29.973
"Think about it," he said. "Reds have been disappearing all over Magica.

71
00:05:29.974 --> 00:05:35.001
Then this weirdo shows up at my house, and suddenly Boz is missing.

72
00:05:35.002 --> 00:05:38.789
The guy has to be involved with whatever the palace was—"

73
00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:47.938
He stopped talking with a gasp as the magic curtain shattered, and a fast-moving figure burst into the cave.

